\newlabel{fig:orgea48f15}{{1}{1}{Overview of the training and evaluation pipeline. Quantum states are measured, reconstructed via tomography, and normalized to unit Frobenius norm. A neural denoiser maps the normalized noisy state to a denoised estimate, which is then projected to a valid density matrix before computing Uhlmann fidelity}{figure.caption.1}{}}
